From: Roman Kuraev <naoru.desu@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Export the versioned libva entry point from the QCOM backend

libva probes the entry point for its current ABI before older versions. Mesa is
linked into this backend and exports its own versioned entry point, so dlsym can
resolve that symbol from Mesa instead of reaching the QCOM backend's 1.0 entry.
Export an alias for the ABI used to build this backend to keep initialization here.

This is a local compatibility fix for the separate qcom-va-driver project.
The base project is MIT-licensed and credits the libva-v4l2 contributors.

Based-on: radxa-pkg/qcom-va-driver 0980a1decf26d34c9aa71cd0a4a0d25703a7a17f
Link: https://github.com/radxa-pkg/qcom-va-driver/tree/0980a1decf26d34c9aa71cd0a4a0d25703a7a17f

diff --git a/src/backend.cpp b/src/backend.cpp
index 56fc3e6..9d7881d 100644
--- a/src/backend.cpp
+++ b/src/backend.cpp
@@ -1308,3 +1308,9 @@ extern "C" VAStatus __vaDriverInit_1_0(VADriverContextP ctx) {
         return VA_STATUS_ERROR_OPERATION_FAILED;
     }
 }
+
+// Look up this backend's entry point before any from the linked Mesa libraries.
+#define IRIS_VA_NAME_I(major, minor) __vaDriverInit_##major##_##minor
+#define IRIS_VA_NAME(major, minor) IRIS_VA_NAME_I(major, minor)
+extern "C" VAStatus IRIS_VA_NAME(VA_MAJOR_VERSION, VA_MINOR_VERSION)(VADriverContextP)
+    __attribute__((alias("__vaDriverInit_1_0")));
